            "numericRating": null,
            "content": "firstly, the dancers, singer and flamenco guitar player were all incredible and deserve a 5/5. There are several levels of payment for example 1. The show and consumption $35 per person 2. The show and tapas $50 person 3. The show and full dinner $70 per person. Look at the pricing online. We paid $70 per person and have the ticket voucher with payment as proof. We received tapas and not the dinner for which we paid for. In the description on line you get wine or a soda AND water. We had two sodas and two waters. In the end we were charged for a soda. Unbelievable. A large group was given all the good seats and everyone else was giving the scraps. This large group also disrupted the artists performing more than once. On a positive, our seats were in the corner and we could not see the full stage. However there were others with worse seats. Rather than trying to pack an abundant amount of people inside for profits they should spend more time making sure the food is hot and that patrons receive the services they pay for. Truly disappointed.",
